## 2. Built-in connectors (1)

Destination batching on `--preview.pipeline-arch-v2`: the engine batches a destination itself with its effective `sdk.batch.size` and `sdk.batch.delay` (the pipeline config, else the connector's own defaults, so S3 is batched at 1000 records / 1s with nothing set) and hands the connector `0` for them, so the connector does not batch as well. It writes a partial batch at the latest `sdk.batch.delay` after its first record, even when no further record arrives (a timer, as in the connector SDK). With `sdk.batch.size` alone a partial batch waits for more records or a stop, and the start logs `pipeline.archv2_destination_batch_unbounded_wait`. A dead-letter queue with `sdk.batch.size` above 1 or `sdk.batch.delay` above 0 is refused with `pipeline.archv2_destination_batching_unsupported`. A destination or dead-letter-queue `sdk.batch.*` value must be a literal: one containing `$` (an environment reference such as `${S3_BATCH}`) is refused with `pipeline.archv2_destination_batching_not_literal`, because the engine batches with the value as written. Runbook: docs/operations/archv2-destination-batching.md.

